 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help with that. 'Not working' can mean a few different things, so I need to know if it's completely dead or just not starting. 1. Is the display lit up? If it is completely blank (no lights at all), try plugging another appliance into that socket to confirm the socket has power.\n2. If there are lights on the display, do any buttons work when you press them, or does the microwave just sit there without responding?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "display is lit, shows the time. buttons just beep but it won't start"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the display is on but it won't run, this is usually a safety feature or a control issue rather than a major electrical fault. Many microwaves have a child lock that stops buttons working even if they beep, and some models refuse to start until the clock time is set. Please check for a lock symbol on the screen (try holding 'Stop' for 3 seconds) and ensure the clock is set. If those are fine, try starting it with a cup of water inside to see if it responds at all."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yes there's a little L symbol on the screen. holding stop for 3 secs made it go away and it works now, thanks"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Child lock was active]\nGlad to hear that sorted it! The 'L' symbol indicates the child lock was on, which prevents the microwave from starting even if the display is lit. You can turn it back on anytime by holding the Stop button for about 3 seconds if you need to keep it safe from accidental use."
  }
 ],
